## Step 6: Macro Expansion

Complex macros with comma operators often fail. Expand them inline.

### Problematic Macro

```glsl
#define m(f, h)\
    s /= (f), \
    p = abs(fract(q/s)*s - s*.5), \
    d = min(d, ...)
```

### Expanded Version

```glsl
// Instead of m(2., 6.):
s /= 2.0;
vec3 mp = abs(fract(q/s)*s - s*.5);
d = min(d, min(max(mp.x, mp.y), min(max(mp.y, mp.z), max(mp.x, mp.z))) - s/6.0);

// Instead of m(2., 4.):
s /= 2.0;
mp = abs(fract(q/s)*s - s*.5);
d = min(d, min(max(mp.x, mp.y), min(max(mp.y, mp.z), max(mp.x, mp.z))) - s/4.0);
```

