## Step 9: Multi-Pass Shaders (Buffers)

Shadertoy uses Buffer A, B, C, D for multi-pass rendering. shader-web-background handles this differently.

### Shadertoy Multi-Pass

```glsl
// Buffer A
void mainImage(out vec4 fragColor, vec2 fragCoord) {
    vec4 prev = texture(iChannel0, fragCoord/iResolution.xy);
    // process
    fragColor = result;
}

// Image (final)
void mainImage(out vec4 fragColor, vec2 fragCoord) {
    fragColor = texture(iChannel0, fragCoord/iResolution.xy);
}
```

### shader-web-background Multi-Pass

**index.html:**
```html
<script type="x-shader/x-fragment" id="my-shader-buffer">
    precision highp float;
    uniform vec2 iResolution;
    uniform sampler2D iChannel0;

    void main() {
        vec2 uv = gl_FragCoord.xy / iResolution;
        vec4 prev = texture2D(iChannel0, uv);
        // process
        gl_FragColor = result;
    }
</script>

<script type="x-shader/x-fragment" id="my-shader-image">
    precision highp float;
    uniform vec2 iResolution;
    uniform sampler2D iChannel0;

    void main() {
        gl_FragColor = texture2D(iChannel0, gl_FragCoord.xy / iResolution);
    }
</script>
```

**JavaScript registration:**
```javascript
ShaderRegistry.register('my-shader', {
    shaders: {
        'my-shader-buffer': {
            uniforms: {
                iResolution: (gl, loc, ctx) => gl.uniform2f(loc, ctx.width, ctx.height),
                iChannel0: (gl, loc, ctx) => ctx.texture(loc, ctx.buffers['my-shader-buffer'])
            }
        },
        'my-shader-image': {
            uniforms: {
                iResolution: (gl, loc, ctx) => gl.uniform2f(loc, ctx.width, ctx.height),
                iChannel0: (gl, loc, ctx) => ctx.texture(loc, ctx.buffers['my-shader-buffer'])
            }
        }
    }
}, 'Description');
```

