## Complete Conversion Checklist

- [ ] Add `precision highp float;` at top
- [ ] Declare all uniforms explicitly
- [ ] Convert `mainImage` to `main()`
- [ ] Replace `fragCoord` → `gl_FragCoord.xy`
- [ ] Replace `fragColor` → `gl_FragColor`
- [ ] Fix `iResolution` type (vec3 → vec2)
- [ ] Convert complex for loops to simple form with break
- [ ] Implement `tanh()` if used
- [ ] Replace `isnan()` with `x != x`
- [ ] Replace `isinf()` with comparison
- [ ] Expand problematic macros
- [ ] Initialize all variables explicitly
- [ ] Fix variable name conflicts
- [ ] Convert `texture()` → `texture2D()`
- [ ] Test and fix any remaining type mismatches

---

## Common Uniform Mappings

| Shadertoy Uniform | Type | JavaScript Setup |
|-------------------|------|------------------|
| `iTime` | `float` | `gl.uniform1f(loc, performance.now() / 1000)` |
| `iResolution` | `vec2` | `gl.uniform2f(loc, ctx.width, ctx.height)` |
| `iMouse` | `vec2` | `gl.uniform2f(loc, mouseX, mouseY)` |
| `iChannel0` | `sampler2D` | `ctx.texture(loc, ctx.buffers['buffer-id'])` |

---

## Debugging Tips

1. **Check browser console** for GLSL compilation errors with line numbers
2. **Simplify first** - comment out complex sections to isolate errors
3. **Test incrementally** - convert one function at a time
4. **Watch for precision** - add `precision highp float;` if seeing artifacts
5. **Variable initialization** - undefined variables cause unpredictable results

